# Research items, wont be committed to the repo
research/

# Handover builds. Every one of these is a whole runtime with the app inside it - the
# self-contained flavour is seventy megabytes - and they are rebuilt from source on demand,
# so nothing is lost by keeping them out and a great deal of repository is saved.
# One pattern rather than a list: a new flavour gets a new folder every few releases, and
# every time it was added by hand after turning up in the changes to commit.
dist/
publish/
publish-*/

# Built mod paks. The app writes these into the game's own Paks folder rather than here, but they
# turn up in the repo the moment somebody exports a zip or stages one to test - and every one is
# rebuildable from the sources beside it, so none of them is worth carrying.
*.pak

# Unreal working directories, in case a project is ever kept under Tools. None of it is source:
# Saved holds the cooked output, Intermediate and DerivedDataCache are caches, Binaries is built.
# The cooked assets that matter are checked in deliberately, as their own files - see below.
Tools/**/Saved/
Tools/**/Intermediate/
Tools/**/DerivedDataCache/
Tools/**/Binaries/
Tools/*

# ...except the generators. These BUILD the cooked assets that ship inside the exe, and
# every one of them carries the reason it is shaped the way it is: why a pivot is not a
# base, why a UMG colour is linear and not sRGB, why a button is tinted through
# BackgroundColor rather than a WidgetStyle, why add_component_to_blueprint must not run
# twice. Shipping the cooked output while the source that made it lives on one machine is
# how a binary becomes unreproducible.
!Tools/loader/
Tools/loader/*
!Tools/loader/*.py
!Tools/loader/*.txt

# The loader's cooked blueprints are SOURCE, and must stay tracked.
#
# They look exactly like build output - four binary Unreal files - and the obvious tidy-up is to
# add *.uasset to this file. That silently breaks the build: MCDSaveEdit.csproj embeds them
#
#     <EmbeddedResource Include="Logic\LoaderAssets\*.uasset" />
#     <EmbeddedResource Include="Logic\LoaderAssets\*.uexp" />
#
# and the app installs the loader by reading them back out of itself. Without them the project
# still compiles and then throws "This build does not carry BP_Tent.uasset" at the one moment
# somebody presses Install loader.
#
# They cannot be regenerated from this repository either. They are cooked in Unreal 4.22 with the
# UnrealEnginePython plugin, from the scripts in Tools/loader, and the editor is not part of this
# project. These four files are the only copy.
#
# The exceptions are written out now so that adding a blanket rule later cannot take them.
!MCDSaveEdit/Logic/LoaderAssets/
!MCDSaveEdit/Logic/LoaderAssets/*.uasset
!MCDSaveEdit/Logic/LoaderAssets/*.uexp

# The item plugin's compiler output. The DLL the app ships is copied out of it by build.bat into
# MCDSaveEdit/Logic/PluginAssets, and THAT copy is tracked: the app embeds it, and building it
# takes the Visual Studio C++ tools, which the app's own build does not need.
ItemPlugin/out/
!MCDSaveEdit/Logic/PluginAssets/*.dll
